DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't bet big before tonight.</b> Stocks rose two days in a row on AI hopes, but the Fed, Microsoft and Alphabet all land within hours (early Thursday Bangkok time). Keep regular investing (DCA) instead of big one-off bets.",
"<b>Oil is calmer, not safe.</b> WTI slipped under $100 on regional peace talks, but the Houthis claimed a hit on a Saudi refinery the same day; higher fuel still feeds inflation and December hike odds above 80%.",
"<b>Spread your risk.</b> AI firms are raising record sums (Meta's oversubscribed $25B share sale, the $63B Anthropic chip deal); broad index funds beat betting on single names into earnings.",
"<b>Cash and short-term bonds still pay.</b> The 10Y is near 5% and the 2Y near 4.7%; short-term deposits and bonds are a fine place to wait.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It is back near $4,060; keep only a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is stuck around $80k; below ~$78k support, expect more downside.",
"<b>Thai investors: hold and be selective.</b> The SET dipped 0.25% to 1,575.02 on DELTA's weak results while foreigners kept buying; brokers see 1,560-1,590 today and a BoT hold at 1.00%. In our dividend table, SPALI, TVO, PTT, ICHI and AP trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 33.6 = Fear (after Tuesday's close), up from 27.3 the day before and 28.7 a week ago, as stocks rose two days in a row and volatility eased; investors are still cautious before the Fed and Big Tech earnings."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~44 = Elevated, about flat: Iran's leader talked about ending the war and regional talks continue, but the Houthis claimed a hit on a Saudi refinery."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 36.4 = fear, but improving: two straight gains pulled the S&P back toward its trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 28.0 = more lows than highs, fear (41 NYSE highs vs 108 lows Tuesday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 27.8 = fear: buying improved but is still narrow."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 28.6 = still lots of protection buying, a fearful sign, but less than last week."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 50.0 = neutral, as volatility calmed with the two-day rally."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 14.6 = bonds have beaten stocks, extreme fear."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 49.8 = neutral: lenders are a bit less nervous."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 62 (down from 64): Iran's Supreme Leader asked for conditions to end the war, but Trump is still weighing strikes after the 3 Nov midterms. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 38 (flat), the biggest weight: the Oleshky truce is holding and was extended across Kherson, but Lavrov says the war will likely continue and escalate."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 68 (up from 66): the Houthis claimed a missile hit Saudi Arabia's biggest refinery and fired five missiles at the kingdom."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 24 (down from 25): Iran, Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan agreed to more talks, and Putin hosted Iran's president."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 24 (flat): no explicit nuclear threats; Putin said Iran's Bushehr nuclear plant work continues."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,723 Tuesday (+0.6%), a second gain led by chip stocks; still a bit below its 22 Oct peak."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. Flat Tuesday (+0.03%) as energy shares fell with oil."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +1.2% Tuesday as chips jumped 3.6%; Microsoft and Alphabet report tonight."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.99% (Tuesday, flat): high, as markets wait for the Fed."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$99.9 settle Tuesday (−1.8%), back under $100 on regional peace talks."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$113.9 (−1.7% Tuesday); it spiked to ~$117 on a reported Saudi refinery strike, then fell back."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.35/gal (AAA, 27 Oct), flat and just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,067: up a second day as lower oil eased inflation fears."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$80.7k = neutral: it is hovering around $80,000 before the Fed; ~$78k is support."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% now; a hike would make borrowing dearer. Decision Thu 1am Bangkok (Wed 2pm ET)."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). Under 10% for 28 Oct (about 93% hold); better than 80% for a hike in December as inflation stays hot."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~102.2 Tuesday, up about 0.4% (DTN), which weighs on oil and gold."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.0 = a weak yen; the BOJ meets 29-30 Oct."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. 1.00%; economists (KResearch, InfoQuest consensus) expect a hold at today's 28 Oct meeting, and Kalshi traders put a hold at ~97%+."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. SET 1,575.02 (−0.25% Tue 27 Oct) as DELTA fell on weak Q3 results while energy and banks held up; brokers see 1,560-1,590 today."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿952M on 27 Oct, their third buy day in a row, cutting October's net selling to about −฿2.6B (SET data via Kaohoon)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
